findings.claim:
FF10's pass condition is only st != 0 plus "incompatible bytecode". lj_bcread.c raises that same error, LJ_ERR_BCFMT, for four header reasons:
- a version byte other than 2;
- unknown flags;
- an FR2 mismatch;
- the FFI flag on a no-FFI build.

FF10 tests the FFI branch only because its fixture differs from BC_PLAIN in byte 4 alone (0x0E vs 0x0A) and FF9 accepts BC_PLAIN in the same run, but FF10 does not check that FF9 passed. Design §1 F24 says the planned bitwise-operator fix must raise BCDUMP_VERSION to 0x80 or higher. Both arrays hard-code 0x02, so after that change FF9 fails and FF10 passes for the version reason. The suite still exits 1 through FF9, so the gap is not silent.
